## Context
/verify on PR #283 (ticket 0230) adherence pass: the newly documented
"install is the only erg verb that mutates outside tickets/" contract
(AGENTS.md Scope confinement paragraph) is asserted in prose but
enforced by nothing. A prose contract with no guard is exactly the
drift class this raid spent wave 1 closing (0234/0235/0236).

## Actions
1. Add a guard test: run each non-install command from the dispatch
   registry in a scratch repo and assert no writes land outside
   tickets/ (snapshot the tree before/after, diff). Alternatively a
   static check over the dispatch registry if runtime probing is
   too coarse.
2. Follow the 0236 meta-test precedent: totality over the registry,
   documented exclusions explicit, negative control included.

## Test
Negative control: a doctored command (or a temp copy of one) that
writes a file at repo root must trip the guard.

## Exit criteria
- [x] Guard fails when a non-install command writes outside tickets/
      (negative control proves it)
- [x] Green on current main
- [ ] make check passes
